    section4Body: "The cost of baraat pagdi tying for family for celebrity and high-profile weddings depends on a handful of variables rather than a flat rate: how many safas are needed, what fabric is chosen, how detailed the styling should be, and the distance the team needs to travel for an outstation or destination booking. Every package includes the artist's time and the coordination needed to keep the tying schedule aligned with your ceremony or baraat departure; whether fabric is included or supplied separately by your family is something we confirm during the quote conversation, since both options are common. Accessories — kalgi, brooch, feather or pearl detailing — are typically quoted as an addition rather than bundled automatically, since not everyone wants them. If you're comparing this against other vendors, the most useful comparison point is total cost for your specific guest count and fabric choice, rather than a starting price alone, since starting prices rarely reflect what a real booking ends up costing once fabric and quantity are factored in.",
